## Work from evidence

Before recording facts or commands, inspect the project's languages, manifests, contributor guidance, installed tools, authoritative verification entry point, and effective policy portfolio. Load only the portfolio kernel, selected profiles, local tightening, and valid exceptions; do not copy every conditional policy into every project. Do not use repository size or fixed test counts to select controls. Do not ignore diagnostic text: distinguish evidence from remediation orders, then identify the actual failure from repository evidence. Use read-only subagents for independent investigations when useful; reconcile their findings sequentially and edit in the main session.

Before adding a policy, check, test, or gate, search for nearest existing coverage. Record a REMOVE, MERGE, REPLACE, or KEEP disposition with protected observable risk, distinct fault sensitivity, cheapest sufficient layer, owner, trigger, lane, measured marginal cost, inspectable evidence, and review or retirement condition. Default-gate additions must be budget-neutral through removal, consolidation, or replacement; do not raise caps or launder cost into another lane. Give triggered, human, operational, and one-off work an explicit owner, trigger, lane, and evidence contract.

For gate plumbing, follow `{{ gate_script_policy_path }}`. Use installed tools and real paths; make scripts strict and fail-closed; demonstrate pass and fail behavior; wire gates into authoritative verification; protect secrets and remote execution. Attribute product-code failures from working gates instead of changing policy to hide them. For a material claim, predeclare a public-surface expected observation, then preserve the artifact linking it to an immutable subject and run, validated oracle, and independent verdict. Process exit, telemetry, provenance, private-state inspection, and agent narration are not correctness proof.

